<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44239" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔκηλος</span></b>  (A), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>
		(cf. Hdn.Gr.<i><span class="en">
			1.161
		</span></i>), 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔκᾱλος</span></b> , (v. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕκηλος</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>free from care, at one's ease</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔκηλος τὰ φράζεαι ἅσσ᾽ ἐθέλῃσθα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					1.554
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὗδον δ᾽ εὔκηλοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					14.479
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>El.</u>
				241
			</span></i> (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡμεῖς μὲν . . πολέας
				τελέοντες ἀέθλους . . , ὁ δ᾽ εὔκηλος</span> . . <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				3.263
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔκηλοι πολέμιζον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					17.371
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔκηλος τότε νῆα θοὴν . .
				ἑλκέμεν ἐς πόντον</span>, i.e. <i>without fear</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Op.</u>
				671
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Merc.</u>
				480
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔ. τέρπου φρένα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pherecr.
					152
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> in Alexandr.
			and later 
				Ep.
			 of things, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νὺξ εὔ.</span>
			<i>still, silent</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				2.166
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πτέρυγες εὔ</span>. <i>steady,
				even</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				2.935
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὖραι εὔ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Opp.
					<u>H.</u>
					4.415
				</span></i>
			. Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λως</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				2.861
			</span></i>.</div>
